// Vendored decorative icons for the "Слова" part-of-speech tiles
// (WordsPartOfSpeechScreen), search-result rows (searchIndex.ts's
// KIND_EMOJI), and category tiles inside other Category screens
// (FlashcardsCategoriesScreen, more to follow — adjectiveCategories.ts,
// categories.ts, grammar.ts). Same approach as tileEmoji.ts (Home tiles):
// Twemoji (jdecked/twemoji fork, graphics CC-BY 4.0, code MIT), raw SVG
// strings, no npm dependency — only these glyphs exist in the bundle,
// nothing else from the library. Covered by the same README/About
// attribution line as tileEmoji.ts (one CC-BY credit for all Twemoji use
// in the app, not per-file).
//
// Contrast checked against bgCard (#2f1d38) for every glyph, same
// standard as the Home tiles:
// - label, palette, running, raisingHand: dominant fills are light/bright
//   (tan/orange/yellow); each has a tiny dark accent (thumbhole, shoe
//   sole, pupils) too small an area to blend with the card.
// - pointing, numbers: no dark tones at all, or a dark tone that's on its
//   own self-contained light/bright backing (numbers' white digits sit on
//   the glyph's own blue square, independent of card color).
// - question: FAILED on later audit — its only fill (#BE1931, deep red) is
//   the entire glyph, 2.49:1 against bgCard (the note below claiming "no
//   dark tones" was wrong). Fixed the same way as hundredPoints: light
//   stroke (#f4ecf7, width 0.6, opacity 0.4) added to both its paths.
// - compass, map: dominant fills are bright (orange/gold/near-white ring,
//   or blue/green paper); each has one small dark/mid accent (needle
//   half, sea deep-blue) too small an area to blend.
// - bullseye: bright red/white/orange rings, no dark tone at all —
//   duplicated on purpose from tileEmoji.ts's former Home-tile glyph
//   (that tile moved to "brain" once bullseye also became the "Відмінки"
//   category here — same icon in two places at once read as if the Home
//   tile pointed at just that one category, not the whole quiz mode).
// - clock: grey ring + near-white face, dark hands as thin lines only —
//   same "thin accent" pattern as compass's needle.
// - ruler, thermometer: dominant fills bright (yellow / light-grey+red);
//   the one dark tone in each is thin tick-mark lines, same "thin accent"
//   pattern as compass's needle — never a filled area.
// - star, seedling: single solid fill each (bright gold / mid-green),
//   no dark tone at all.
//
// - firstPlaceMedal: dominant fill bright orange/gold disc (8.27:1); ribbon
//   and small "1" numeral accents are darker but too small an area / sit on
//   the bright disc itself, not against bgCard directly.
// - keycapOne..keycapSeven: same blue-square-with-white-digit pattern as
//   numbers (4.06:1 square, 15.51:1 digit) — deliberately reused fill, not
//   a new color choice.
// - hundredPoints: FAILED the check — single solid dark-red fill (#BB1A34,
//   2.45:1 against bgCard), no light/bright element anywhere in the glyph
//   (unlike every other entry above). Same class of problem as
//   graduationCap in tileEmoji.ts — fixed the same way: a light stroke
//   (#f4ecf7, width 0.6, opacity 0.4) on the path, not a recolor.
//
// Never hand-edit path geometry — only re-fetch the same glyph from the
// official repo if the pin needs updating.

